# Salt Meridian, an original orchestral piece in 7/8 by Iceman Free (iceman-free) & SZ.
# Form: beacon, gathering (two strains), ascent, drift, fracture hocket, return, hammered climax,
# afterglow, and collapse. A lone oboe measures the line over a low drone; pizzicato and tubular
# bells fix the 2+2+3 pulse; brass cuts in with answering shards; the middle thins, breaks into a
# hocket, and returns transformed before the full weight arrives and then falls away to a single bell
# and the last note of the oboe.
title: Salt Meridian
composer: Iceman Free & SZ
about: An original piece in F# minor and 7/8: an oboe traces a stark melody over pizzicato pulses, tubular bells, and timpani, brass answers in hard shards, the music thins and fractures into a hocket before returning transformed, a hammered climax follows, and a long afterglow collapses to a lone bell and the oboe's last note.
year: 2026
source: original
category: originals
style: orchestral
key: F# minor
tempo: 138
time: 7/8

